This project establishes a Big Data pipeline to analyze Twitter (X) sentiment and public opinion regarding the English Premier League (EPL) during the critical transition between the 2019/20 and 2020/21 seasons. The system orchestrates a robust architecture using Apache Kafka for resilient data ingestion, Apache Spark for real-time distributed processing and sentiment impact calculation, and PostgreSQL for structured storage. The processed data is visualized through interactive Grafana dashboards, which track dynamic polarity, compare digital impact against league standings, and cross-reference individual player performance with team media presence. The findings reveal compelling insights, demonstrating that a club's digital impact is often driven more by its global fanbase and viral controversies than by its actual sporting success.
